{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings","id":990754,"title":"Question About The Supernal Beings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-20T19:20:04-07:00","id":990754,"title":"Question About The Supernal Beings","content":"Can they exist at the same in more than one realm in Second edition? I know Imperial Mysteries mentioned they could. Na example they Gave was the Hunter In Green. An supernal god representing predation. The Hunter exists in both Stygia and Primal Wild. At least that's what i remember. Is that still holds true in this new edtition?<br /> <br /> Also a somewhat related question. i start wondering something when i read that sidebar on dark eras<br /> <br /> &quot;Generations of sorcery have given some magical<br /> environments and Verges stronger but more specific<br /> Supernal ties than usual. To take advantage<br /> of such places, a sorcerer must invoke the place\u2019s<br /> legends with appropriate images, verses, and<br /> ritual actions. To raise Troy\u2019s ghosts, sing of the<br /> wrath of Achilles!<br /> This goes beyond the normal semiotic associations<br /> mages use to activate Yantras. The sorcerer<br /> performs something resembling a play or mystery<br /> rite to unlock the power of the myth. Learning<br /> the correct rite requires a Prime Unveiling spell<br /> or research via Intelligence + Academics (with a<br /> modifier based on the place\u2019s fame or obscurity).<br /> Once the sorcerer knows what to do and takes the<br /> time to do it, she may use Environment and Action<br /> Yantras, but immediately gains a point of Mana<br /> (that she may spend on the spell, or not, as she<br /> wishes) and enjoys a -1 die penalty to Paradox&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bIf a legend can be used to make magic stronger does that mean that those who were in said legend are in the supernal realms? Meaning can i summon Achilles with the proper ritual?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T19:41:40-07:00","id":990762,"title":"","content":"The thing about Imperial Mysteries is that archmages interact with the supernal realms in a different way than regular mages, so while something might be cosmologically true, it's not necessarily helpful to a street-level summoner. That being said, I could totally imagine a Moros doing a Death+Life summoning, and a Thyrsus doing a Life+Death summoning, and ending up calling down the same Hunter in Green entity (or facets of the same entity from a different point of view, but keeping the memories of when the other mage summoned it.)<br /> <br /> The Achilles thing kind of depends on your point of view. The Diamond (and Seers) would argue that the mortal life and subsequent legend of Achilles were reflections of a pre-existing supernal symbol of a flawed hero, and so invoking the human legend helps connect you to the deeper truth. The Free Council would argue that the life and legend of Achilles <i>created </i>that symbol, and it didn't exist before, so you are directly calling upon Achilles in the supernal realm.<br /> <br /> You could probably summon a Supernal being of Fate or maybe Forces that strongly resembled and embodied Achilles, along with various other similarly flawed champions, and get it to punch your enemies for you (if it will come out of its damn tent). You could absolutely summon the Astral embodiment of Achilles from the Temenos as a goetia. You might even be able to conjure up the shade of a certain very, very old Greek warrior from the Underworld, and you wouldn't be the first mage over the milennia to pester him. It's up to you whether any of these are really the man himself, but they're probably close enough for most of the reasons you'd want to summon Achilles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T20:12:19-07:00","id":990772,"title":"","content":"Let's use an Exarch as an example. Technically, they reside in the Supernal, but they're able to create Ochemata so powerful that it renders the distinction meaningless.<br /> <br /> I would imagine The Hunter in the Green to be similar. There's a Supernal entity, but he has &quot;servants&quot; in the Shadow who are able to act and speak authoritatively in his name as if they were one and the same. Plus, being his version of Ochemata would in fact be shards of himself, so in a sense they are him. They might be slightly less powerful, but on the scale in consideration that wouldn't be enough to create any meaningful distinction.<br /> <br /> Next question, are legends in the Supernal? That's up to your discretion as an ST. There are certainly Symbols that correspond to what you're invoking, but what the distinction between those symbols and the reality are gets left up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T04:28:32-07:00","id":990892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=990762#post990762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about Imperial Mysteries is that archmages interact with the supernal realms in a different way than regular mages, so while something might be cosmologically true, it's not necessarily helpful to a street-level summoner. That being said, I could totally imagine a Moros doing a Death+Life summoning, and a Thyrsus doing a Life+Death summoning, and ending up calling down the same Hunter in Green entity (or facets of the same entity from a different point of view, but keeping the memories of when the other mage summoned it.)<br /> <br /> The Achilles thing kind of depends on your point of view. The Diamond (and Seers) would argue that the mortal life and subsequent legend of Achilles were reflections of a pre-existing supernal symbol of a flawed hero, and so invoking the human legend helps connect you to the deeper truth. The Free Council would argue that the life and legend of Achilles <i>created </i>that symbol, and it didn't exist before, so you are directly calling upon Achilles in the supernal realm.<br /> <br /> You could probably summon a Supernal being of Fate or maybe Forces that strongly resembled and embodied Achilles, along with various other similarly flawed champions, and get it to punch your enemies for you (if it will come out of its damn tent). You could absolutely summon the Astral embodiment of Achilles from the Temenos as a goetia. You might even be able to conjure up the shade of a certain very, very old Greek warrior from the Underworld, and you wouldn't be the first mage over the milennia to pester him. It's up to you whether any of these are really the man himself, but they're probably close enough for most of the reasons you'd want to summon Achilles.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some evidence that the shade and the goetia might be reflections of the original supernal symbol,right?<br /> I was under the impression that anything that can be used as a yantra exists somewhere in the realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T04:30:47-07:00","id":990893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=990772#post990772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's use an Exarch as an example. Technically, they reside in the Supernal, but they're able to create Ochemata so powerful that it renders the distinction meaningless.<br /> <br /> I would imagine The Hunter in the Green to be similar. There's a Supernal entity, but he has &quot;servants&quot; in the Shadow who are able to act and speak authoritatively in his name as if they were one and the same. Plus, being his version of Ochemata would in fact be shards of himself, so in a sense they are him. They might be slightly less powerful, but on the scale in consideration that wouldn't be enough to create any meaningful distinction.<br /> <br /> Next question, are legends in the Supernal? That's up to your discretion as an ST. There are certainly Symbols that correspond to what you're invoking, but what the distinction between those symbols and the reality are gets left up to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>DaveB once said that when they took over the Exarchs dethroned various gods and created an human centric verse. One could argue mortal stories about god's and monsters are people really rembering the Time before","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T05:00:40-07:00","id":990901,"title":"","content":"It could certainly also be that, multiple interpretations are valid on this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T05:03:49-07:00","id":990903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=990901#post990901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could certainly also be that, multiple interpretations are valid on this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>There also this group of archmaster trying bring some gods back to help with their ascension","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:51:14-07:00","id":991074,"title":"","content":"A question that arose in my head as a result of comments elsewhere makes me wonder just what the hell Supernal beings even are. The increasing focus on the Supernal not as a place but as the principals by which reality operates makes the existence of thinking beings somehow &quot;within&quot; it all the harder to grasp conceptually.<br /> <br /> What is a Supernal being? An idea in the mind of God? A supernatural force given form and a clearer semblance of agency? If they're described as living symbols, what does it mean for a symbol to live?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:00:21-07:00","id":991077,"title":"","content":"Hm, my idea for it was that Supernal magic deals with truths, right? You could see it as something that makes the impossible possible, or that turns symbols into reality. If you think of the Supernal as a place of infinite potential energy and meaning, then a Mage can create a bridge between it and reality. (The difference between this and other forms of magic is what makes Paradox and the Abyss flourish. You could see it in a few different ways. Making the impossible possible is itself a paradox that damages reality, or you could see it as the Abyss hitching a ride on the path the Mage makes between the Supernal and reality). <br /> <br /> Of course, the Supernal isn't really a place, and part of what mages do that lets them directly interact with it is that they impose order on it, arranging raw symbols into forms that reality can interact with. Thinking of the Supernal as a place is itself an example of this: normally, contacting the Supernal or attempting to &quot;enter&quot; it completely destroys anyone or anything who tries it, but the five realms forcibly arrange the symbols of the Supernal into a location that the person can interact with. <br /> <br /> So, Supernal Beings. My best understanding of them is that they are as much created as summoned when a Mage summons one, because what the Mage is doing is grabbing a cluster of Supernal symbols and imposing order on them, coalescing them into a defined form. So a Mage who summons a Fate entity that resembles an elven sage isn't actually opening a door to a parallel realm where elves live, she's reaching into a well of raw potential and pulling raw Fate itself into our world, where it is shaped into a coherent form- in this case, an elven sage, because the symbols attached to that form have symbolic connections to the idea of fate.<br /> <br /> Of course, one could argue that an actual True Fae is still technically an &quot;entity of fate&quot;, it's just one that (to hazard a guess) is &quot;native&quot; to the phenomenal world and already represents an embodiment of the concept. The practical difference between the two is that it would probably be easier and safer to summon a Supernal entity than try to cut a deal with the Gentry. I see no reason why a Mage couldn't do that, given that even normal mortals can potentially summon and deal with the Gentry, but &quot;don't fuck with the True Fae&quot; is probably something that gets hammered into any Mage who expresses an interest in messing with fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-21-2016, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:11:33-07:00","id":991078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991074#post991074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question that arose in my head as a result of comments elsewhere makes me wonder just what the hell Supernal beings even are. The increasing focus on the Supernal not as a place but as the principals by which reality operates makes the existence of thinking beings somehow &quot;within&quot; it all the harder to grasp conceptually.<br /> <br /> What is a Supernal being? An idea in the mind of God? A supernatural force given form and a clearer semblance of agency? If they're described as living symbols, what does it mean for a symbol to live?</div> </div> </div> </div>My tke is that they are what give meaning to the world they hav this symbiotic relationship with everythig. But at the same time they are also in many way like people. they have lives, a identity and name. Sometime they even love or hate something. Maybe some of them are not even aware about how much they mean to mages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:21:03-07:00","id":991082,"title":"","content":"Another way to frame the question: What is a Supernal being doing when it's not summoned into the Fallen World?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:33:17-07:00","id":991088,"title":"","content":"I think all you really need to ask to figure that out is, &quot;What are the Exarchs doing?&quot; The Exarchs are at the top tier of the Supernal, and although they're intruders into the Supernal they are also Symbols now. They've appropriated the ability to send things from the Supernal, hence the proliferation of Profane Urim and that includes Supernal Entities, better known as Ochemata. Exarchs presumably maintain the symbols of Tyranny that keep their pantheon propped up and also their personal visions of it via observation, or fear of the other, or what have you. So other Supernal entities probably serve the same purpose for their respective pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:38:13-07:00","id":991092,"title":"","content":"My personal interpretation is &quot;nothing&quot;, since Supernal beings (at least, I would think) only exist as coherent entities when they're summoned into the Phenomenal. When they're in the Supernal, they're just part of the undifferentiated soup of symbols and concepts. Shapes and forms and limits and all of that are what the Phenomenal world uses to give meaning to the Supernal. There are realms where the Supernal is stronger than the Phenomenal (Arcadia, the Hedge, the Underworld, the Astral, and so on being examples), and realms where it's weaker or absent (the Lower Depths), but the Supernal itself, if you think of it as a place, is like the sun: a massive singularity of energy and concepts burning so brightly that individual forms can't coalesce within it, unless they use some sort of framework like the Watchtowers that lets them force the raw elemental chaos into a coherent form they can perceive and interact with. The Supernal and the Phenomenal/Fallen need each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T13:38:58-07:00","id":991093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991082#post991082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to frame the question: What is a Supernal being doing when it's not summoned into the Fallen World?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/573230-supernal-entity-interaction-question?p=575953#post575953\">I've asked this and never really gotten a clear response</a>. Lots of guesses based on the Exarchs, but the Exarchs are a special case as they actively interfere in the Fallen World.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:12:36-07:00","id":991103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991082#post991082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to frame the question: What is a Supernal being doing when it's not summoned into the Fallen World?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they interat with other. Pray symbols are eaten by predator symbols. Angels fight their wars. The dead rest in peace","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:15:41-07:00","id":991104,"title":"","content":"See, the problem with that is that is makes the Supernal into too much of a defined place for me, and it also steps on the toes of the assorted other lines. The Shadow is where predator symbols eat prey symbols, it's the Shadow's hat. The Underworld is where the dead go. To give another example, if Supernal Arcadia is literally just a dimension with elves and stuff, that makes Phenomenal Arcadia kind of redundant, plus the unfortunate &quot;the Supernal world is the Fallen world but better and purer&quot; idea, which I really don't think 2e is supporting much.<br /> <br /> To go more into the narrative purpose argument, and away from Watsonianism, the problem with the Supernal being a place where &quot;predator symbols eat prey symbols&quot; from a worldbuilding and storytelling standpoint is that the game already has a perfectly fine and fleshed out place where embodiments of predation eat embodiments of prey, and it has the bonus of being a place that mages can travel too fairly easily that you can easily work into campaigns and adventures. <br /> <br /> The Watsonian argument against it would what I mentioned earlier, about how the Supernal is a formless sea of potential without the Phenomenal to shape it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-21-2016, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T14:25:23-07:00","id":991114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991104#post991104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Watsonian argument against it would what I mentioned earlier, about how the Supernal is a formless sea of potential without the Phenomenal to shape it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's how the Abyss is sometimes described. Or close to it. It's endless possibility that just can't exist because something already exists in its place that contradicts it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T19:25:58-07:00","id":991223,"title":"","content":"The Underworld is where ghosts go, and they're not usually considered more than an echo of the dead. As far as Mages know, no one knows what happens to the dead.<br /> <br /> That aside, the symbol soup idea has some merit. Maybe the Exarchs expected to find gods when they invaded and the symbols to create gods coalesced and the Exarchs took those primordial symbol soup gods and kicked them out. Then in that case Mages are performing a similar function when they call down a Supernal entity, but are constrained to those entities that can be created by the symbols found in their Paths, and obviously, on a much smaller scale.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Watchtowers and their surrounding &quot;environs&quot; being a special case much like the Exarchs -that is an artificial construct forced on the Supernal by outsiders-, Supernal entities summoned from them might in fact have functions and existences that extend beyond simply being summoned into the Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T03:17:23-07:00","id":991322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991082#post991082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to frame the question: What is a Supernal being doing when it's not summoned into the Fallen World?</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess is &quot;nothing.&quot; I don't think Supernal entities (barring Exarchs and other Ascended) meaningfully exist when you aren't looking at them. Ever since Dave made it clear that the Supernal isn't a place so much as a level of being that is immanent in the Fallen, and that Prime is the Arcanum of Truth, I've conceived of it as a sort of magical holodeck, a stage populated by bits of code that act in ways defined by their nature and which emulate consciousness without &quot;really&quot; possessing it. In this view, the act of summoning is more like running a program (defined by the summoner's spell and powered by their mana) than bringing an entity from &quot;there&quot; to &quot;here.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T03:29:23-07:00","id":991324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991223#post991223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, the Watchtowers and their surrounding &quot;environs&quot; being a special case much like the Exarchs -that is an artificial construct forced on the Supernal by outsiders-, Supernal entities summoned from them might in fact have functions and existences that extend beyond simply being summoned into the Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. Aside from the Exarchs and whatever the Watchtowers are, we know there are many Ascended mages (doesn't each Exarch command 777 Arch-Ascended?) so even if Supernal entities are mere simulacra that only exist when maintained by a conscious mind, there are certainly plenty of minds to run them. Maybe a sufficiently long-lived program can even be tainted by enough of the Phenomenal to become a real being in its own right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T11:08:11-07:00","id":991457,"title":"","content":"So, after ruminating on the question for a few days and reading everyone's answers, my own response has coalesced.<br /> <br /> My take on Supernal entities has to be that they're not really entities at all, in the typical sense of the word. They are more akin to demesnes or Verges or Emanation Realms; manifestations of Supernal law, in an exceptionally narrow and confined manner.<br /> <br /> The Supernal is not a separate universe or other worlds or another plane of being - at least, not in the classical sense of being able to imagine it as a place filled with objects and places you can walk about in. It is the structure of reality; it is the aggregated symbols that give the universe form and meaning. Symbols are things for which any action is an expression of itself. That is, a symbol is a Platonic essence; The Thing Itself. It cannot be meaningfully subdivided.<br /> <br /> Symbols, thus, do what their nature commands; interacting with all other symbols to produce reality. The Exarchs send dreams and visions and trinkets because it is what an Exarch does; the Tyrant is not a Tyrant if it does not command its lessers. Storms manifest around destruction, for it is what storms do. Cats are graceful and everyone senses the presence of feline grace even in entirely different species, because the very idea of a Cat is bound into grace intimately.<br /> <br /> So when summoning a Supernal entity, one is not pulling out a symbol or creating an entity or what have you; one is simply emphasizing and enhancing a Supernal symbol's influence over a segment of reality; just as one might with a spell, save with exceptional clarity and purity. This singular symbol is given control over a localized region of reality and it does what symbols do when given control: It changes the world around it. The way it does so is by shaping the reality it's been given influence over. When it does so, this just inevitably means it takes on forms and shapes sufficient to appear as an entity.<br /> <br /> But it's not the symbol. It's just the symbol given more influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:27:51-07:00","id":991503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991082#post991082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another way to frame the question: What is a Supernal being doing when it's not summoned into the Fallen World?</div> </div> </div> </div>My take would be: something we can't understand.<br /> <br /> For me, summoning is not coalescing symbols as much as cutting parts of greater symbols and mixing them up. But the &quot;greater&quot; symbol stays active. A mage needs to do it that way because he can't understand the full scope of a true Supernal symbol.<br /> <br /> For instance, when you call upon a supernal being in the form of three ladies with a single eye, you do not take &quot;death&quot; and &quot;fate&quot; and make them into people. You take one tiny part of Fate, one tiny part of Death and mix them into something adequate for your mind to grasp without your brain melting through your ears. (And that explains why, for instance, you can have Fate as an arcanum and Fate as it is understood by the changelings)<br /> <br /> So the summons are created by the mage's mind to be able to interact with the symbol power. But in the supernal, the symbols act according to their true nature which is far beyond anything your street level mage can understand. And for me the division between symbols is, in part, arbitrary: &quot;death&quot; and &quot;life&quot; aren't opposite symbols. They are opposite &quot;poles&quot; on a spectrum that comprises a greater symbol. Think of it as your average country: inside the country, several lobbies will try to stir the country in some way. Businessmen will try to lower the taxes while public servant will try to have more money for their work. So they might appear, to someone who look at a street level, as opposed to each other as it is posible. But if you look at the level of a chief of state, a coherence and a dynamic appear. So for me, in the Supernal, symbols are acting in ways human can barely understand and in accordance to their nature, while respecting a sort of equilibrium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T18:09:24-07:00","id":991638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lokiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991503#post991503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My take would be: something we can't understand.<br /> <br /> For me, summoning is not coalescing symbols as much as cutting parts of greater symbols and mixing them up. But the &amp;quot;greater&amp;quot; symbol stays active. A mage needs to do it that way because he can't understand the full scope of a true Supernal symbol.<br /> <br /> For instance, when you call upon a supernal being in the form of three ladies with a single eye, you do not take &amp;quot;death&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;fate&amp;quot; and make them into people. You take one tiny part of Fate, one tiny part of Death and mix them into something adequate for your mind to grasp without your brain melting through your ears. (And that explains why, for instance, you can have Fate as an arcanum and Fate as it is understood by the changelings)<br /> <br /> So the summons are created by the mage's mind to be able to interact with the symbol power. But in the supernal, the symbols act according to their true nature which is far beyond anything your street level mage can understand. And for me the division between symbols is, in part, arbitrary: &amp;quot;death&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;life&amp;quot; aren't opposite symbols. They are opposite &amp;quot;poles&amp;quot; on a spectrum that comprises a greater symbol. Think of it as your average country: inside the country, several lobbies will try to stir the country in some way. Businessmen will try to lower the taxes while public servant will try to have more money for their work. So they might appear, to someone who look at a street level, as opposed to each other as it is posible. But if you look at the level of a chief of state, a coherence and a dynamic appear. So for me, in the Supernal, symbols are acting in ways human can barely understand and in accordance to their nature, while respecting a sort of equilibrium.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is how I like to picture it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:16:04-07:00","id":991918,"title":"","content":"A side question of some interest to me on this topic would be: if the symbols that you summon into being on the Fallen World have no real existence of their own in the Supernal, what do we think happens if you summon the same set of symbols more than once? Do they recognize this mage that keeps calling on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:36:16-07:00","id":991925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Midgardener</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991918#post991918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A side question of some interest to me on this topic would be: if the symbols that you summon into being on the Fallen World have no real existence of their own in the Supernal, what do we think happens if you summon the same set of symbols more than once? Do they recognize this mage that keeps calling on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I sure Hope soo. The idea that they don't have identities and histories is sort boorring too mme","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:19:50-07:00","id":991943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Midgardener</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991918#post991918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A side question of some interest to me on this topic would be: if the symbols that you summon into being on the Fallen World have no real existence of their own in the Supernal, what do we think happens if you summon the same set of symbols more than once? Do they recognize this mage that keeps calling on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see why they wouldn't, any more than a rock would be missing the nicks and scratches from tumbling down a hill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T12:33:20-07:00","id":991951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991077#post991077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My best understanding of them is that they are as much created as summoned when a Mage summons one, because what the Mage is doing is grabbing a cluster of Supernal symbols and imposing order on them, coalescing them into a defined form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's entirely accurate. It seems like they have their own &quot;lives&quot;, so to speak, their own purposes and things going on, and that's why it's such a Wisdom crime to let them die in this world.<br /> <br /> The Hunter in Darkness is certainly not someone who disappears when no one is looking at him.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the entire point of Ascension is to no longer be dependent on the whims of Fallen Reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:14:24-07:00","id":992002,"title":"","content":"Even if that is what the writers' intent was, I wouldn't personally go with that. ChroD already has so many realms of supernatural beings going about their business that adding another one (not to mention establishing it as &quot;higher&quot; or &quot;better&quot; than the other ones) doesn't really feel right to me. Plus, I've always thought of Ascension as a negative thing, equivalent to becoming one of the True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:17:59-07:00","id":992006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992002#post992002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if that is what the writers' intent was, I wouldn't personally go with that. ChroD already has so many realms of supernatural beings going about their business that adding another one (not to mention establishing it as &quot;higher&quot; or &quot;better&quot; than the other ones) doesn't really feel right to me. Plus, I've always thought of Ascension as a negative thing, equivalent to becoming one of the True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<img src=\"https://media.tenor.co/images/bb0ba736217a35d5e62371950693f2b5/raw\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:21:59-07:00","id":992010,"title":"","content":"Hey, nothing's saying you have to go with that. There Is No Canon. I'm just saying that I personally don't like that take on it. If you have an objection to my objection, I would be happy to hear it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T14:48:45-07:00","id":992030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992010#post992010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, nothing's saying you have to go with that. There Is No Canon. I'm just saying that I personally don't like that take on it. If you have an objection to my objection, I would be happy to hear it.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bno not really,i was just surpised. besides i love a excuse to show of a Bojack giff","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 10-23-2016, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T15:22:07-07:00","id":992056,"title":"","content":"Hopefully the answers will be in Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T16:27:12-07:00","id":992096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992056#post992056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully the answers will be in Signs of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Th3 firstly chapter if I recall","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T17:12:34-07:00","id":992114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992002#post992002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if that is what the writers' intent was, I wouldn't personally go with that. ChroD already has so many realms of supernatural beings going about their business that adding another one (not to mention establishing it as &quot;higher&quot; or &quot;better&quot; than the other ones) doesn't really feel right to me. Plus, I've always thought of Ascension as a negative thing, equivalent to becoming one of the True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we actually talke about that: Supernal isn't better, it just is different.<br /> <br /> We should think about &quot;the supernal as a place where people live&quot; as a mc Guffin. What does it tell about the world, what does it give to the story, ... ? For me, it gives a plot device to further one of my views about the game world: in the supernal everything is related to everything and is a degraded version of an original principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12295-lokiel","name":"Lokiel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T23:46:29-07:00","id":992283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=991104#post991104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the problem with that is that is makes the Supernal into too much of a defined place for me, and it also steps on the toes of the assorted other lines. The Shadow is where predator symbols eat prey symbols, it's the Shadow's hat. The Underworld is where the dead go. To give another example, if Supernal Arcadia is literally just a dimension with elves and stuff, that makes Phenomenal Arcadia kind of redundant, plus the unfortunate &quot;the Supernal world is the Fallen world but better and purer&quot; idea, which I really don't think 2e is supporting much.<br /> <br /> To go more into the narrative purpose argument, and away from Watsonianism, the problem with the Supernal being a place where &quot;predator symbols eat prey symbols&quot; from a worldbuilding and storytelling standpoint is that the game already has a perfectly fine and fleshed out place where embodiments of predation eat embodiments of prey, and it has the bonus of being a place that mages can travel too fairly easily that you can easily work into campaigns and adventures.<br /> <br /> The Watsonian argument against it would what I mentioned earlier, about how the Supernal is a formless sea of potential without the Phenomenal to shape it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shadow is a dim reflection of the truth of the Primal Wild. The Underworld is a dim reflection of Stygia. Fallen Arcadia is a dim reflection of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> The storytelling purpose of it is perfect - the Shadow isn't a virtuous cycle. The Underworld is a shithole. Fallen Arcadia is a monstrous trap.<br /> <br /> All of these things are indicative of the way the world is <i>broken,</i> something that's fundamental to the Gnostic theme of Mage. If you feel like this puts the Splat on a higher level of primacy than the others - knda tough? You're allowed to rewrite it of course, but that's on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:36:55-07:00","id":992318,"title":"","content":"Saying that it's higher is basically just a way to say that it's more refined or rarified. The Supernal is like Carbon, it's in practically everything (Things are derived from it) and there are expressions of pure carbon that are considered more valuable than anything else. That doesn't necessarily make it &quot;better&quot; than Oxygen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T07:03:51-07:00","id":992365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992283#post992283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shadow is a dim reflection of the truth of the Primal Wild. The Underworld is a dim reflection of Stygia. Fallen Arcadia is a dim reflection of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> The storytelling purpose of it is perfect - the Shadow isn't a virtuous cycle. The Underworld is a shithole. Fallen Arcadia is a monstrous trap.<br /> <br /> All of these things are indicative of the way the world is <i>broken,</i> something that's fundamental to the Gnostic theme of Mage. If you feel like this puts the Splat on a higher level of primacy than the others - knda tough? You're allowed to rewrite it of course, but that's on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jachra Dave Brookshaw made a point of reminding everyone the two Arcadias ain't related","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:46:38-07:00","id":992398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992365#post992365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jachra Dave Brookshaw made a point of reminding everyone the two Arcadias ain't related</div> </div> </div> </div>Did he?<br /> <br /> I know he says they're not the same thing, but I don't know if he said they're not related at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T08:58:57-07:00","id":992401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992398#post992398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did he?<br /> <br /> I know he says they're not the same thing, but I don't know if he said they're not related at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar14_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"14\" data-vbnamecard=\"14\">Dave Brookshaw</a>. Did you confirmed the two arcadias are not related?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:10:19-07:00","id":992406,"title":"","content":"He posted a few possibilities (not official canon) about what Fae-Arcadia might be in the other currently active Supernal thread. One of the possibilities had the two Arcadias connected. The official stance is simply that they are not the same realm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990170-question-about-supernal-realms-vs-other-realms?p=990341#post990341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The contract-based nature if changeling reality and the appearance of the Hedge might suggest some connection to Supernal Arcadia even if they're not the same (Mage-Arcadia's &quot;thorns&quot; look like silver cracks in reality, the name being an apt description that confuses first-time crossover readers). Perhaps, then, Faerie-and-the-Hedge is a particularly large and active Emanation Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:25:14-07:00","id":992415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992406#post992406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He posted a few possibilities (not official canon) about what Fae-Arcadia might be in the other currently active Supernal thread. One of the possibilities had the two Arcadias connected. The official stance is simply that they are not the same realm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAhh. Sorry jachra i was wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:39:55-07:00","id":992420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992283#post992283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shadow is a dim reflection of the truth of the Primal Wild. The Underworld is a dim reflection of Stygia. Fallen Arcadia is a dim reflection of Arcadia.<br /> <br /> The storytelling purpose of it is perfect - the Shadow isn't a virtuous cycle. The Underworld is a shithole. Fallen Arcadia is a monstrous trap.<br /> <br /> All of these things are indicative of the way the world is <i>broken,</i> something that's fundamental to the Gnostic theme of Mage. If you feel like this puts the Splat on a higher level of primacy than the others - knda tough? You're allowed to rewrite it of course, but that's on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think these things need to be dim reflections of something else to be falling short of an ideal. The Supernal gives a glimpse of what could be, perhaps should be, but it isn't any of those things.<br /> <br /> The idealized Shadow is not the Primal Wild; it is a more virtuous Shadow, free from the cold dog-eat-dog violence of the Raptor and the blind catastrophe of the Nemesis; a virtuous, self-sustaining, ever-improving cycle but ultimately still the Shadow, not the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> The Primal Wild contains these ideals, these possibilities... But it also contains the Raptor and Nemesis. It is also not a place. It is not the place Awakened should aspire to and seek to escape to or bring here; it is the sum of the symbols that make reality and tell the Awakened what is possible.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Supernal is not an idealized version of the Fallen World; it merely contains the symbolic possibility of a world that is not Fallen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T09:53:32-07:00","id":992429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992420#post992420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think these things need to be dim reflections of something else to be falling short of an ideal. The Supernal gives a glimpse of what could be, perhaps should be, but it isn't any of those things.<br /> <br /> The idealized Shadow is not the Primal Wild; it is a more virtuous Shadow, free from the cold dog-eat-dog violence of the Raptor and the blind catastrophe of the Nemesis; a virtuous, self-sustaining, ever-improving cycle but ultimately still the Shadow, not the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> The Primal Wild contains these ideals, these possibilities... But it also contains the Raptor and Nemesis. It is also not a place. It is not the place Awakened should aspire to and seek to escape to or bring here; it is the sum of the symbols that make reality and tell the Awakened what is possible.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Supernal is not an idealized version of the Fallen World; it merely contains the symbolic possibility of a world that is not Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good way to see things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T10:44:07-07:00","id":992470,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Again, this is all opinion and personal canon, and whatever you prefer world for you, but the &quot;dim reflection&quot; idea would only work for me if I were going for a completely Mage-centric cosmology. (Though it is a view that I can see a lot of mages holding)<br /> <br /> My personal view on the realms isn't that, for example, Stygia is &quot;the underworld but better&quot;, but that it's a form that mages force onto the raw potential of the Supernal so that they can interact with it without being destroyed or subsumed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:44:50-07:00","id":992510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992420#post992420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think these things need to be dim reflections of something else to be falling short of an ideal. The Supernal gives a glimpse of what could be, perhaps should be, but it isn't any of those things.<br /> <br /> The idealized Shadow is not the Primal Wild; it is a more virtuous Shadow, free from the cold dog-eat-dog violence of the Raptor and the blind catastrophe of the Nemesis; a virtuous, self-sustaining, ever-improving cycle but ultimately still the Shadow, not the Primal Wild.<br /> <br /> The Primal Wild contains these ideals, these possibilities... But it also contains the Raptor and Nemesis. It is also not a place. It is not the place Awakened should aspire to and seek to escape to or bring here; it is the sum of the symbols that make reality and tell the Awakened what is possible.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Supernal is not an idealized version of the Fallen World; it merely contains the symbolic possibility of a world that is not Fallen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a better way to put it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Again, this is all opinion and personal canon, and whatever you prefer world for you, but the &quot;dim reflection&quot; idea would only work for me if I were going for a completely Mage-centric cosmology. (Though it is a view that I can see a lot of mages holding)<br /> <br /> My personal view on the realms isn't that, for example, Stygia is &quot;the underworld but better&quot;, but that it's a form that mages force onto the raw potential of the Supernal so that they can interact with it without being destroyed or subsumed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an interpretation of direct evidence. Ignoring it displays willful ignorance.<br /> <br /> If you dislike Gnosticism, sure, fine, but don't expect the canon to back you up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:50:08-07:00","id":992515,"title":"","content":"Technically, you're both right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T11:51:03-07:00","id":992517,"title":"","content":"Okay, sure. I don't think I'm displaying &quot;willful ignorance&quot; when I've seen plenty of other people agree that the Supernal Realms are not &quot;better higher versions of the other dimensions&quot;, but ultimately each person has their own preferences and canon. I'm only talking about my own preference, as are you. You believe that your canon is the same or closer to the canon of the developers, and that may be true. <br /> <br /> And I don't dislike gnosticism, and it should be noted that Mage having very gnostic themes doesn't mean that there isn't room to interpret the setting from a holistic crossover point of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T14:43:26-07:00","id":992578,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Mage has beaucoup Gnosticism flowing through it but it's not orthodox in its Gnostic leanings. My loose understanding is that most of the early Gnostics saw the world as-is as something created by the Demiurge; flawed and incomplete and ultimately illusory; something to be overcome so one might transcend and rejoin the One. Mage, on the other hand, has reality as most certainly real and directly emanating from the only thing that can come close to being called God. The Fallen World is Fallen, but it's also still the World; it's not unnatural or undesirable, merely broken.<br /> <br /> If you like individuality, experience, and life in general, the World is great. It's the Fallen part that buggers it up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:16:09-07:00","id":992609,"title":"","content":"Given that magic is supposed to be alive (at least according to the Mysterium and possibly the Free Council as well), as well as the fact that there are multiple references to living symbols, I'd say that it is both a separate dimension filled with objects and entities as well as the structure of the Fallen World. The Exarchs don't seem to be alone in their self agency among supernal beings. Also, to me ascension is meaningless without continued self awareness and self agency.<br /> <br /> I'm also particularly tired atm, so I'll finish these thoughts later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:55:46-07:00","id":992634,"title":"","content":"Arguably you maintain agency and lose self-awareness or your former consciousness is otherwise rendered completely alien. This isn't helped by the fact that any memories of your past un-Ascended self would be rendered semi-to full on incoherent by the fact that your Ascended self has always and will always exist and the act of Acension has a ripple effect on reality which would make the previous iteration of it completely different than what your pre-Ascension self was familiar with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-24-2016, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T16:55:52-07:00","id":992635,"title":"","content":"The Mysterium believes magic is alive in the sense of it being an active, self-directing force; it responds and reacts, rather than blindly acting the same way over and over. It doesn't mean that these things take the shape of creatures or entities in another dimension or realm. Which isn't to say they also couldn't, but... Eh. It's not contingent that they are, is the thing.<br /> <br /> Likewise, Ascension isn't meaningless without continued self-awareness or agency - plenty of people have died trying to change the world, after all - but I don't think that is what is being said here either. Self-awareness and agency don't have to be the type or character we're familiar with for them to be there. For example, if a Supernal being is the symbol it is bound to, it can't really want or choose to be or do anything but what it is; the Exarchs will always be tyrants because there is no part of them that is anything else; everything superfluous beyond that is burned away in the light of being the very idea of tyranny. Yet the Exarchs are still ostensibly active actors; directing things according to their natures.<br /> <br /> It's not easy or natural to think of a self-directing law of nature - how, after all, could one imagine gravity to be sapient? - but it's not unfathomable either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T13:09:08-07:00","id":993060,"title":"","content":"I think it's entirely possible that Ascending means that the being in question surrenders its ability to act in ways contrary to its nature, though it remains &quot;thinking&quot; and &quot;aware&quot; or some analogous state of being. I don't think that, for instance, an Exarch could stop acting to further tyranny even if it/he/she somehow wanted to. This seems to go hand in hand with the theme (which we already see in Imperial Mysteries regarding Archmasters) that gaining power, paradoxically, curtails one's freedom of action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T22:26:48-07:00","id":993324,"title":"","content":"That <i>is</i> a fun theme. Ties into the whole notion that power lies in becoming The Thing Itself, which is threaded throughout Mage in things like Shadow Names and the Law of Sympathy and such-like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T03:54:39-07:00","id":993414,"title":"","content":"If you guys ask me,Asceinding doesn't has any element of losing. you only gain. Because when you ascend you become a symbol of magic,a symbol fop yourself. So everything you are,your hopes and dreams and memories and feelings is forever and ever immortalized","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:44:02-07:00","id":993577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jacobkosh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=993060#post993060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's entirely possible that Ascending means that the being in question surrenders its ability to act in ways contrary to its nature, though it remains &quot;thinking&quot; and &quot;aware&quot; or some analogous state of being. I don't think that, for instance, an Exarch could stop acting to further tyranny even if it/he/she somehow wanted to. This seems to go hand in hand with the theme (which we already see in Imperial Mysteries regarding Archmasters) that gaining power, paradoxically, curtails one's freedom of action.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe that's accurate. There's even an ascended being mentioned, or at least one of the subsouls they send down. - the only thing constraining the actions of an Ascended being is another Ascended being. They appear to have their own goals, motivations, needs.<br /> <br /> Archmasters similarly have goals and dreams and, always, are <i>more</i> of themselves, not less. It's just that the rest of the universe wants to act to prevent them from having a free hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=992517#post992517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, sure. I don't think I'm displaying &quot;willful ignorance&quot; when I've seen plenty of other people agree that the Supernal Realms are not &quot;better higher versions of the other dimensions&quot;, but ultimately each person has their own preferences and canon. I'm only talking about my own preference, as are you. You believe that your canon is the same or closer to the canon of the developers, and that may be true.<br /> <br /> And I don't dislike gnosticism, and it should be noted that Mage having very gnostic themes doesn't mean that there isn't room to interpret the setting from a holistic crossover point of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Supernal being the purest origin of the world doesn't necessarily mean that crossover potential is dead. Power Stat 6+ beings are perfectly able to survive in the Supernal (see: Imperial Mysteries) and they have patrons that exist up there. Arguably, before the world Fell, they might well have used Supernal powers since they were much more accessible back then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-26-2016, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:47:48-07:00","id":993580,"title":"","content":"(Accidental double post)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T14:53:28-07:00","id":993716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=993414#post993414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you guys ask me,Asceinding doesn't has any element of losing. you only gain. Because when you ascend you become a symbol of magic,a symbol fop yourself. So everything you are,your hopes and dreams and memories and feelings is forever and ever immortalized</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, that might not be the case. Symbols are, to borrow an Aquinian ideal, pure essence. That is, they are the essential parts of that idea, indivisible and inseparable, and nothing more. If you become a symbol of something, any part of you that <i>doesn't</i> align with that symbol simply wouldn't exist anymore. Not that it'd bother you, though, since it'd never have existed in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=993577#post993577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe that's accurate. There's even an ascended being mentioned, or at least one of the subsouls they send down. - the only thing constraining the actions of an Ascended being is another Ascended being. They appear to have their own goals, motivations, needs.<br /> <br /> Archmasters similarly have goals and dreams and, always, are <i>more</i> of themselves, not less. It's just that the rest of the universe wants to act to prevent them from having a free hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of this is contradictory to the idea that they surrender the possibility of self-contradiction. Goals, motivations, and needs can emanate from having a defined nature. The Exarchs are the perfect example: They are incarnate tyrants who have goals, motivations, and needs entirely within the context of being tyrants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jachra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=993577#post993577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power Stat 6+ beings are perfectly able to survive in the Supernal (see: Imperial Mysteries) and they have patrons that exist up there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Citation very much needed, unless you're talking about Supernal entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:16:09-07:00","id":993728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=993716#post993716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Citation very much needed, unless you're talking about Supernal entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 51. It's more an implication than a direct statement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each Supernal Realm contains the undiluted energy of true Creation: a mystical torrent powerful enough to strip virtually any soul it of its independent identity. After the Awakening, no mage below the rank of archmaster may enter the Supernal Realms. If a lesser mage somehow finds himself in the Supernal, his soul is immediately claimed by the Realm. The mage dies or is transformed into a lesser Supernal entity under the control of the Storyteller. Rumors speak of mages\u2019 bodies returning with new inhabitants, such as Ochemata, or extensions of Old Ones. <b>All other beings with supernatural power traits of 5 of less are irrevocably destroyed.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T15:51:34-07:00","id":993751,"title":"","content":"That is curious. I get the feeling that's not meant to mean that a Blood Potency 6 Vampire can just walk out of an Archmaster's Supernal sanctum and whistle a happy tune, though. Thanks for sourcing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T16:01:30-07:00","id":993753,"title":"","content":"There's the bit about a lesser mage's soul being claimed by the Realm. I think that would apply to all Power Trait 6+ entities, except maybe, just maybe, beings that has Rank as their Power Trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T18:15:30-07:00","id":993816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/990754-question-about-the-supernal-beings?p=993716#post993716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, that might not be the case. Symbols are, to borrow an Aquinian ideal, pure essence. That is, they are the essential parts of that idea, indivisible and inseparable, and nothing more. If you become a symbol of something, any part of you that <i>doesn't</i> align with that symbol simply wouldn't exist anymore. Not that it'd bother you, though, since it'd never have existed in the first place.<br /> None of this is contradictory to the idea that they surrender the possibility of self-contradiction. Goals, motivations, and needs can emanate from having a defined nature. The Exarchs are the perfect example: They are incarnate tyrants who have goals, motivations, and needs entirely within the context of being tyrants.</div> </div> </div> </div>The essential idea of yourself?<br /> <br /> Basic immunity to self-contradiction is already a thing with the appropriate use of Mind magic. That's no more than saying that their will and intelligence are such that they can't be tripped up by mortal problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>All other beings with supernatural power traits of 5 of less are irrevocably destroyed.</b> </div> </div> </div>Power traits is really not ambiguous. Power traits are several times defined as the splat's power stat.<br /> <br /> Why mages aren't immune above 5 is less clear, unless it means the fact that archmages have a minimum Gnosis of 6. I don't think so, though - the Archmage supertemplate is a qualitatively different life than a standard issue mage.<br /> <br /> It may be that mages being more open to it makes them more vulnerable.<br /> <br /> I seriously doubt life would be EASY for such a werewolf/vampire. I'd imagine over time they might end up becoming an inhabitant, since it's doubtful there's a way home for them that isn't through an archmage or a somehow-friendly Ascended being.<br /> Maybe you could draw them back with a summoning ritual and ask the denizen to bring them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 10-26-2016, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}